"Too often, when participating in a social discussion, we do not genuinely listen to our interlocutor; we merely wait for our turn to speak.",
"We prepare our own counter-arguments in our minds instead of assimilating the emotional nuances and subtle details of the discourse being addressed to us.",
"This total lack of authentic attention constitutes the primary source of personal misunderstandings that weaken our relational structures, both amical and professional.",
"Listening truly requires that one temporarily set aside one's own biases and judgments to understand another individual's perspective.",
"It does not imply that you must systematically approve of everything that is expressed, but that you make an effort to welcome their thought with respect.",
"Experts in social psychology affirm that practicing active listening stimulates the production of empathy and immediately calms rising tensions during a conflict.",
"Forvu that we learn to remain silent and observe non-verbal signals carefully, we will discover a human dimension of unexpected richness.",
"In the final analysis, knowing how to listen is a generous gesture that validates the existence of others and solidifies mutual trust long-term."
